     Demonstration data.

     Scope of this file, and the reason for that scope:

     This file ships only master data that can be created without naming a
     single record outside this module. Demonstration batches, batch records,
     stability studies, serialised units and dossiers are deliberately absent,
     for two independent reasons.

     First, each of them needs at least one external identifier that could not
     be verified against the Odoo 19 source from the build environment: a
     demonstration product of the "product" module, or a unit of measure of
     the "uom" module. A "ref" attribute that does not resolve aborts the
     installation of the whole module, so naming an unverified identifier here
     would put installation at risk in exchange for sample data.

     Second, a batch release decision must pass the guards implemented in
     ls.pharma.batch.release, which check the state of the batch, the approval
     of its batch records, the presence of an expiry date and the separation
     between the person who manufactured the batch and the person who decides
     on it. A decision written directly as an XML record would bypass exactly
     the controls that this module exists to enforce, and would leave the
     batch and its decision in states that contradict each other.

     The full scenario, from a planned batch through execution, review,
     release and serialisation, is built instead by the test suite in
     ls_pharma/tests, where the records are created through the ORM and a unit
     of measure is found by searching the database rather than by naming it.
-->
<odoo>
    <data noupdate="1">

        <record id="demo_api_paracetamol" model="ls.pharma.api">
